      ":question/id": "596c3e80-0a77-5c0b-9dd5-ac5db525f1a6",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\frac{1}{8}}{\\sqrt{1 - 64 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the linear substitution $u=8 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=8,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{8})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\frac{1}{8}}{\\sqrt{1 - 64 x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\frac{1}{8}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(8 x)^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{8}(\\frac{1}{8})\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{64}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(u \\right)}}{64}+C \\\\  &= \\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}{\\left(8 x \\right)}}{64}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
